WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
- So wait, so tell us

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.450
about this new version of West Side Story.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.400
- Well, I think it's
really important to note

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.130
that it is a re-imagination.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.100
It is so not a remake.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.150
This thing is a masterpiece
and it stands on its own.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:12.983
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:12.983 --> 00:00:15.720
But I love that we are
retelling a classic story

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.210
for a new generation, you know

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.883
Steven Spielberg and Tony Kushner.

00:00:21.883 --> 00:00:24.410
I realized that maybe I'm
a little too comfortable

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.250
since I just called

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.450
one of the greatest directors of all time

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:27.390
by his first name.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.750
- Well, you worked with him for a minute.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.340
I think you probably were
on a first-name basis.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.350
Yeah.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.420
- But he and Tony Kushner

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.268
and our casting director Cindy Tolan

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:38.530
paid, you know, great attention to detail.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.360
And there there's such
a beautiful commitment

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.658
to authentic casting here.

00:00:42.658 --> 00:00:45.326
Every Latino is played by a Latino.

00:00:45.326 --> 00:00:46.159
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:00:46.159 --> 00:00:48.231
- It's really, it's really cool.

00:00:48.231 --> 00:00:51.170
I mean, you can't beat the dance numbers.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.660
Just the music is just, it's
really something to behold.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.490
So I hope y'all will give
it a chance and go see it.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.934
- I love that he did this.

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.290
I think it's so cool.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.630
So Rita Moreno originated
the role of Anita,

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:02.490
the character that you played.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:03.970
So did you get to meet her?

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:05.080
Was that nerve wracking?

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.433
- I did.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.610
- What does that mean?

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.070
That could go either way for me.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:10.960
- No, no, no.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.240
She came to, to do kinda
like a show and tell day.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.073
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:16.073 --> 00:01:17.380
- Where she spoke to the entire cast

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.490
and talked about her experience
with making the '61 film,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.030
et cetera et cetera.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.040
And she's telling this fabulous story

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:28.250
and she says, wait, where is
the girl that plays Anita?

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.670
Where is Ariana?

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.233
And she was like, niña,
we got some talking to do.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.260
And I proceeded to have
a massive anxiety attack.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.120
I hid under the bleachers
until like 30 minutes later

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.030
I finally found the courage to be like,

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.530
I'm so sorry I'm so awkward,

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.930
but I'm really happy to meet you.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.340
And, and she was like,

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.710
I'll tell you anything you wanna know.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.930
And I said, I wanna know
anything you wanna tell me.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.320
And she said, lean into
everything that makes you unique

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.570
and you don't need my help.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:57.450
You've got this.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.620
- Oh, I love that.

00:01:59.823 --> 00:02:02.352
That's special. Okay.

00:02:02.352 --> 00:02:04.768
I'm so excited to see this and hear it

00:02:04.768 --> 00:02:06.162
and experience it.
- I hope you like it.

00:02:06.162 --> 00:02:07.240
- I'm gonna love it.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.190
This is right up my alley

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.150
- The reviews are bananas.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.501
Like we're our household is
flipping out to see this thing.

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:12.651
- [Kelly] Yeah
- Yeah.

